# PREDICTION for ROOT lane run 15, committed ALONE and BEFORE the run.
#
# STEP -1 of `scratch/lane-run-7-procedure.md`. The derivation is written out so it is
# checkable independently of whether the number matches. That is not decorative: R19-06 and
# R20-07 are two runs whose FIGURE was right and whose EXPLANATION was reconstructed
# afterwards, and D0A-R26-06 made it three — in the run-14 prediction, in this very file. The
# number matching is not evidence the reasoning was right.
#
# ORDERING IS CONVENTION, NOT MECHANISM (D0A-R22-01, reopened). `git log` on this file versus
# the result file is the only evidence the prediction came first. It held for runs 13 and 14.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY RUN 15 IS OWED
#
# Run 14 closed D0A-R24-01 and its freshness check was real. But it ran at `af6dde0`, BEFORE
# the round-26 remediation, which added five tests and changed four security-relevant paths:
# the tier ceiling (Confirm, not Biometric), the deadline-bounded read, the CLOCK_BOOTTIME
# consent window, and the configurable read ceiling. None of that has executed at root.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DERIVATION
#
# Base: run 14 measured EXECUTED 187 / SKIPPED 5 / reported 192 at root (freshness MEASURED:
#       sha256 over all 17 executables before and after a forced rebuild, `diff` empty).
#       The current unprivileged pair is EXECUTED 172 / SKIPPED 25 / reported 197 (measured
#       2026-09-06 at bd15ffb, re-measured by the pre-commit hook across all 17 targets).
#
# Delta since run 14: the round-26 remediation added FIVE tests and removed none. Each was
# checked for root-gating BY GREP of its body — geteuid, a SKIP branch, a bwrap_available
# guard, a path-existence branch — not from memory:
#
#   service.rs       biometric_is_refused_..._no_biometric_factor            no gate
#   store.rs         boot_secs_reads_the_boottime_clock_...                  no gate
#   canonicalize.rs  a_read_that_does_not_return_is_refused_by_the_deadline  no gate
#   canonicalize.rs  work_that_completes_within_the_deadline_is_not_refused  no gate
#   canonicalize.rs  a_malformed_ceiling_is_refused_rather_than_defaulted    no gate
#
# ALL FIVE UNGATED — cleaner than run 14's derivation, which had one path-existence branch
# (`/usr/bin/coreutils`) to reason about. Nothing here depends on euid, on a filesystem, or on
# a facility root has differently.
#
# So:  187 + 5 = 192 EXECUTED.  The root skip set is UNCHANGED at 5:
#   b1_daemon_binary                      needs --features insecure-test-seams
#   an_unreadable_login_defs              this uid can read a 0000 file          (root-caused)
#   a_regular_login_user_is_not_refused   running as root                        (root-caused)
#   pidfd_refuses_a_recycled_pid_barrier  userns unavailable to root here        (root-caused)
#   live_logind_query                     standing DEFER
#
# CONSISTENCY CHECK, because both lanes must describe the SAME test set:
#   unprivileged  172 + 25 = 197 reported
#   root          192 +  5 = 197 reported
# A `reported` other than 197 means the test SET changed, not the skip distribution — a
# different defect from a count mismatch, to be diagnosed as such.
#
# Root and unprivileged remain OVERLAPPING SETS, neither a superset: three of the five root
# skips execute unprivileged. 192 > 172 is NOT a coverage claim.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE ONE TEST WITH A TIMING-DERIVED TOLERANCE — named in advance so a failure is diagnosed
# rather than re-run
#
# `boot_secs_reads_the_boottime_clock_and_does_not_go_backwards` asserts two CLOCK_BOOTTIME
# reads differ by at most 1 second (the sampling gap). Under a heavily loaded serial root run
# that tolerance is the only thing in the five that could fail for a reason unrelated to its
# property. If it fails, check the elapsed wall time of the run before concluding anything
# about the clock — and per Iron Law #15 clause 5, DEMONSTRATE the harness explanation rather
# than assuming it.
#
# `a_read_that_does_not_return_is_refused_by_the_deadline` uses a 150 ms deadline against a
# 60 s sleep — a 400x margin, in the direction where load makes it MORE likely to fire
# correctly, so it is not in the same category.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RESIDUALS THIS RUN CARRIES BUT CANNOT CLOSE — recorded here because a residual kept only
# beside the fix that created it gets read as part of that fix
#
# 1. THE SUSPEND DIVERGENCE IS UNMEASURED, NOT VERIFIED. R26-03 moved the consent window to
#    CLOCK_BOOTTIME because CLOCK_MONOTONIC pauses across suspend. This box has never
#    suspended (BOOTTIME - MONOTONIC = 0.000s), so NO assertion available on this lane
#    distinguishes the two clocks, and the test that exists checks clock IDENTITY. A green run
#    15 does NOT verify the suspend behaviour. Do not let the record imply otherwise.
#
# 2. THE PENDING STORE HAS NO CAP. The read ceiling bounds ONE proposal at 2x; nothing bounds
#    accumulation. It is adjacent to what R26-04 just fixed, which is exactly how it will be
#    mistaken for closed. Invisible today (B1 services one action and exits); live when B2
#    loops.
#
# 3. `argv` IS EMPTINESS-CHECKED ONLY, while `env_delta` is NUL-checked at both doors. Raised
#    in the round-26 prompt; the findings did not answer it. A question a reviewer declined to
#    answer reads as settled unless it is recorded as unanswered. It is unanswered.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A MISMATCH IS A RESULT. Record which side was wrong. Do not adjust this derivation until it
# agrees with the measurement.

EXPECTED_EXECUTED=192
EXPECTED_SKIPPED=5
EXPECTED_REPORTED=197
